  "description": "T1. Common Walnut\tRear Garden:\rSelectively reduce crown height and spread by 2m, pruning the longer \rstem sections back to suitable growth points to leave a natural, rounded \rappearance; these works are to help mitigate a modest 10% lean.\rRemove dead branches throughout the crown area that are over 2.5cm in \rdiameter, and inspect the crown for any adverse conditions.\r\rT2. Mulberry Tree\tRear Garden:\r\rTree Assessment and Recommended Works:\rDue to age and fractures in the main trunk,  a stem has shifted \rfurther over the lawn as a result of a partial collapse.\rTo help preserve this splendid Victorian Mulberry tree, \rI recommend the following works:\rReduce back branches currently spread across the lawn to the \rborder of the shrub bed.\rReduce the over-extended stem by 3.5m to improve stability \rand balance of the crown.\rRemove or stabilise dead branches throughout the crown.",
